      "writtenOn": "2019-04-27T00:48:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the decision if dut-contol supplied device or /dev/ttyUSBx will be used  should be done in one place.\n\ntechnically speaking hadcoding /dev/ttyUSB{0..2} is not guaranteed to work - I often have other USB to FTDI dongles plugged in, this messes up SuzyQ device assignment.\n\nIdeally proper /dev/ttyUSB needs to be discovered automatically, at least there should be a command line option to override the base device number, the rest should be derived from the base as +1 and +2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 2
      },
